  bootwright / preflight clusters
      Check the readiness of the selected OpenShiftClusters and CephClusters: the checks of
      preflight container-cluster and of preflight storage-cluster, reported together.
      --clusters takes names of either kind, and a cluster of neither kind is refused. The SSH
      and trust-on-first-use options apply to the CephCluster checks; the OpenShiftCluster
      checks observe the controller and take none.

  Usage
    bootwright preflight clusters [flags]

  Command flags
      --clusters            Select comma-separated cluster names (default: all)
      --dry-run             Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --trust-on-first-use  Observe unknown SSH keys without accepting them · default true

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright preflight clusters --context lab --output json
